<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Pius VI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1717–1799</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Giovanni Angelo Braschi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pius VI, born Giovanni Angelo Braschi, was pope from 1775 to 1799. He condemned the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>'s Civil Constitution of the Clergy, and in 1797 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> forced him to cede the Legations by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tolentino">Treaty of Tolentino</a>. When the French proclaimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-republic">Roman Republic</a> in 1798 he was taken prisoner and died in exile at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valence">Valence</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vi.jpg" alt="Pope Pius VI" width="320" height="445" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pompeo Batoni · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pompeo_Batoni_-_Ritratto_di_Papa_Pio_VI_(National_Gallery_of_Ireland).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
